From 74e78591a3694f1e63db0a29c0424651ae737149 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Bowen Wang <wangbowen1001@yahoo.com>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 20:50:03 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] [Benchmark] Report goodput and SLO attainment in
 bench_serving

Add --goodput KEY:VALUE pairs (ttft, tpot, e2el, in milliseconds; the
spelling vLLM's benchmark uses). A request is good if it succeeded and met
every listed SLO. The run then reports request goodput (good requests per
second), SLO attainment over all requests sent, and one attainment per
listed SLO, in the console output and in the result file. Without the flag
the output and the result fields are unchanged.

The scoring lives in sglang/benchmark/goodput.py; serving.py parses the
option, calls it and reports the result.
